1581
00:56:51,000 --> 00:56:52,160
 And then--

1582
00:56:52,160 --> 00:56:54,600
 I've never had that happen.

1583
00:56:54,600 --> 00:56:55,520
 I've never had that happen.

1584
00:56:55,520 --> 00:56:58,760
 Well, I was telling him, I have a friend that was mad at me

1585
00:56:58,760 --> 00:57:01,040
 because I had him do a film.

1586
00:57:01,040 --> 00:57:02,960
 And he's not really an actor, but he's phenomenal.

1587
00:57:02,960 --> 00:57:06,560
 But if you're watching this, I know you're still mad at him.

1588
00:57:06,560 --> 00:57:07,760
 He's like, when's that film?

1589
00:57:07,760 --> 00:57:09,120
 I also know you're still mad at him.

1590
00:57:09,120 --> 00:57:10,720
 Yeah, when's the film coming out?

1591
00:57:10,720 --> 00:57:12,360
 And I'm like, dude, I'm not the director.

1592
00:57:12,360 --> 00:57:13,720
 It's your friend who got you on it.

1593
00:57:13,720 --> 00:57:14,400
 But some people--

1594
00:57:14,400 --> 00:57:15,800
 More importantly, the director doesn't even

1595
00:57:15,800 --> 00:57:17,640
 have any impact on the film going out.

1596
00:57:17,640 --> 00:57:20,320
 And one more thing that you said about--

1597
00:57:20,320 --> 00:57:23,320
 I think surviving LA is going to be a really good thing for people

1598
00:57:23,320 --> 00:57:25,760
 to understand when you are here.

1599
00:57:25,760 --> 00:57:29,360
 The one thing that wasn't mentioned that is huge

1600
00:57:29,360 --> 00:57:36,840
 is you will have to meet people that have worked so hard to get

1601
00:57:36,840 --> 00:57:37,560
 where they're at.

1602
00:57:37,560 --> 00:57:40,640
 And you will have to meet people that just got here.

1603
00:57:40,640 --> 00:57:42,720
 And they get the craziest roles.

1604
00:57:42,720 --> 00:57:46,920
 And you will watch people who've been here forever skyrocket.

1605
00:57:46,920 --> 00:57:48,680
 And they're 20 years of being here.

1606
00:57:48,680 --> 00:57:50,440
 Now they're huge actors.

1607
00:57:50,440 --> 00:57:53,240
 And within five minutes, you could

1608
00:57:53,240 --> 00:57:55,280
 be the biggest actor or actress.

1609
00:57:55,280 --> 00:57:59,440
 So that in between is far and few.

1610
00:57:59,440 --> 00:58:00,440
 You just have to do it.

1611
00:58:00,440 --> 00:58:01,440
 You have to keep going.

1612
00:58:01,440 --> 00:58:04,320
 But there's a hell of a lot more people that don't make it.

1613
00:58:04,320 --> 00:58:06,080
 Yeah, I was lucky.

1614
00:58:06,080 --> 00:58:09,200
 When I got here, I guess start on happy days,

1615
00:58:09,200 --> 00:58:11,160
 two days after I got here.

1616
00:58:11,160 --> 00:58:12,720
 Do you see what I'm saying?

1617
00:58:12,720 --> 00:58:14,040
 That's incredible.

1618
00:58:14,040 --> 00:58:17,640
 Yeah, and I'd never been to LA before.

1619
00:58:17,640 --> 00:58:21,280
 But I knew I'm so grateful to one of the producers,

1620
00:58:21,280 --> 00:58:22,400
 William S. Bickley.

1621
00:58:22,400 --> 00:58:23,240
 Bill Bickley.

1622
00:58:23,240 --> 00:58:24,320
 Thank you, William.

1623
00:58:24,320 --> 00:58:26,040
 And I'd gone to high school with him.

1624
00:58:26,040 --> 00:58:28,160
 So I just simply gave him a call.

1625
00:58:28,160 --> 00:58:30,120
 And I said, hey, Bill, it's Susie.

1626
00:58:30,120 --> 00:58:33,000
 And I guess that's what everybody called me back then.

1627
00:58:33,000 --> 00:58:35,520
 And he said, well, come over to Paramount.

1628
00:58:35,520 --> 00:58:38,160
 And so I went out and had lunch with me.

1629
00:58:38,160 --> 00:58:39,120
 Welcome to LA.

1630
00:58:39,120 --> 00:58:40,240
 So I go over.

1631
00:58:40,240 --> 00:58:41,560
 And he takes me on the set.

1632
00:58:41,560 --> 00:58:44,560
 And Henry Winkler comes and goes, oh, yeah, who are you?

1633
00:58:44,560 --> 00:58:48,200
 And so Henry said something like, make up my girlfriend.

1634
00:58:48,200 --> 00:58:50,760
 And so they wrote me in that week.

1635
00:58:50,760 --> 00:58:51,880
 Get out of here.

1636
00:58:51,880 --> 00:58:54,040
 And so Henry and I went out.

1637
00:58:54,040 --> 00:58:55,440
 We're really good friends.

1638
00:58:55,440 --> 00:58:57,680
 I'm a huge fan of Henry.

1639
00:58:57,680 --> 00:59:00,520
 Now, I have to tell you, of all the people

1640
00:59:00,520 --> 00:59:01,800
 I've ever met in LA--

1641
00:59:01,800 --> 00:59:02,960
 He's wonderful.

1642
00:59:02,960 --> 00:59:04,080
 He's the sweetest man.

1643
00:59:04,080 --> 00:59:05,360
 Yes, I've heard a lot about him.

1644
00:59:05,360 --> 00:59:07,480
 He is the sweetest man in Hollywood.

1645
00:59:07,480 --> 00:59:08,400
 He really is.

1646
00:59:08,400 --> 00:59:09,240
 He really is.

1647
00:59:09,240 --> 00:59:10,920
 You're all about reputation.

1648
00:59:10,920 --> 00:59:12,680
 I always talk about reputation.

1649
00:59:12,680 --> 00:59:15,240
 It's something like, look, that's another thing

1650
00:59:15,240 --> 00:59:17,720
 you have to keep your reputation because everybody

1651
00:59:17,720 --> 00:59:20,000
 remembers everything that ever has come from you.

1652
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:22,840
 Yeah, you know, I guess maybe sometimes I

1653
00:59:22,840 --> 00:59:25,320
 was a little bit prima donna, I suppose.

1654
00:59:25,320 --> 00:59:28,320
 But it's not a good idea to do that.

1655
00:59:28,320 --> 00:59:33,240
 I told-- I've told many of my friends this.

1656
00:59:33,240 --> 00:59:34,840
 You still a baby actor.

1657
00:59:34,840 --> 00:59:37,560
 Yeah, so I explain to everybody just,

1658
00:59:37,560 --> 00:59:39,640
 even if you're acting on the set or you're

1659
00:59:39,640 --> 00:59:42,560
 doing something on set, there's a thing called set etiquette.

1660
00:59:42,560 --> 00:59:43,960
 No matter who you are, right?

1661
00:59:43,960 --> 00:59:46,000
 Because it's a functioning thing.

1662
00:59:46,000 --> 00:59:47,840
 And one of the things you had mentioned,

1663
00:59:47,840 --> 00:59:49,760
 which it just always blew my mind,

1664
00:59:49,760 --> 00:59:52,920
 was somebody had given up--

1665
00:59:52,920 --> 00:59:54,880
 let's say all of a sudden production has an actor

1666
00:59:54,880 --> 00:59:56,680
 and they can't act or somebody gets hurt.

1667
00:59:56,680 --> 00:59:59,160
 They have to replace that person, right?

1668
00:59:59,160 --> 01:00:02,400
 It is a lot to replace people and to get them in there.

1669
01:00:02,400 --> 01:00:04,160
 And it's like, let's say you're doing a stunt

1670
01:00:04,160 --> 01:00:06,520
 and I'll never forget this.

1671
01:00:06,520 --> 01:00:08,880
 When I first-- I got this list and they asked me

1672
01:00:08,880 --> 01:00:10,000
 all the things I can do.

1673
01:00:10,000 --> 01:00:14,560
 And I was about to check off surfing and something else

1674
01:00:14,560 --> 01:00:15,080
 and my friend--

1675
01:00:15,080 --> 01:00:16,280
 You're leading your resume, didn't you?

1676
01:00:16,280 --> 01:00:18,880
 So my friend looked over and he goes, don't do that.

1677
01:00:18,880 --> 01:00:20,080
 And I was like, what do you mean?

1678
01:00:20,080 --> 01:00:23,040
 I can learn how to ride a unicycle.

1679
01:00:23,040 --> 01:00:24,080
 He's like, what do you mean?

1680
01:00:24,080 --> 01:00:25,760
 I go, I found one at the thrift store.

1681
01:00:25,760 --> 01:00:26,080
 I have it.

1682
01:00:26,080 --> 01:00:27,960
 He goes, can you actually ride a unicycle?

1683
01:00:27,960 --> 01:00:29,120
 I was like, no, but I can practice.

1684
01:00:29,120 --> 01:00:30,080
 He goes, take that check.

1685
01:00:30,080 --> 01:00:30,880
 Take it out, yeah.

1686
01:00:30,880 --> 01:00:31,720
 Yeah, so like--

1687
01:00:31,720 --> 01:00:32,680
 You'll break your neck.

1688
01:00:32,680 --> 01:00:35,600
 Well, you'll get hired to ride that unicycle.

1689
01:00:35,600 --> 01:00:38,320
 And then, yes, so that's just another good piece

1690
01:00:38,320 --> 01:00:39,120
 of information.

1691
01:00:39,120 --> 01:00:41,080
 I was just on a-- I just had a national commercial

1692
01:00:41,080 --> 01:00:42,240
 a couple of weeks ago.

1693
01:00:42,240 --> 01:00:44,160
 And one of the--

1694
01:00:44,160 --> 01:00:46,120
 I guess she's considered kind of a stunt girl,

1695
01:00:46,120 --> 01:00:49,400
 but she was there in like a little soccer scene.

1696
01:00:49,400 --> 01:00:51,960
 And she actually broke her ankle.

1697
01:00:51,960 --> 01:00:53,800
 And they had to find somebody the next day.

1698
01:00:53,800 --> 01:00:55,960
 She broke her ankle on rehearsal day, so think--

1699
01:00:55,960 --> 01:00:58,520
 Which happens more than I'm actually on shooting day.

1700
01:00:58,520 --> 01:01:00,920
 Listen, people get hurt on sides.

1701
01:01:00,920 --> 01:01:01,800
 I know, I'm so sad.

1702
01:01:01,800 --> 01:01:03,000
 She's such a sweetie, too.

1703
01:01:03,000 --> 01:01:05,200
 I'll look up your name, but you're amazing.

1704
01:01:05,200 --> 01:01:06,040
 I mean, people--

1705
01:01:06,040 --> 01:01:07,240
 Hope you're doing OK.

1706
01:01:07,240 --> 01:01:09,360
 --think that it's easy, physically.

1707
01:01:09,360 --> 01:01:11,160
 I work out every day.

1708
01:01:11,160 --> 01:01:14,120
 And because you've got to be--

1709
01:01:14,120 --> 01:01:15,720
 you've got to be kind of strong.

1710
01:01:15,720 --> 01:01:17,800
 You've got to be either on your feet--

1711
01:01:17,800 --> 01:01:19,000
 Standing up all the time.

1712
01:01:19,000 --> 01:01:22,320
 It's standing up a lot and making your mark.

1713
01:01:22,320 --> 01:01:23,920
 And that's why you have to study.

1714
01:01:23,920 --> 01:01:27,320
 I think it's really good to study acting.

1715
01:01:27,320 --> 01:01:28,840
 I had a really good question here.

1716
01:01:28,840 --> 01:01:31,040
 And it was something to do with making your mark.

1717
01:01:31,040 --> 01:01:33,560
 It said, Pat Hingle taught you a trick on Barnaby

1718
01:01:33,560 --> 01:01:36,280
 Jones for hitting your mark without looking down.

1719
01:01:36,280 --> 01:01:40,040
 What else do old pros teach you that nobody teaches now?

1720
01:01:40,040 --> 01:01:41,120
 I saw this question.

1721
01:01:41,120 --> 01:01:42,680
 I was like, wow, that's a good one.

1722
01:01:42,680 --> 01:01:43,520
 Kidding the mark.

1723
01:01:43,520 --> 01:01:47,160
 I was theater trained, though I was in the union.

1724
01:01:47,160 --> 01:01:51,320
 I joined SAG when I was about 18 or 17, 17 or 18.

1725
01:01:51,320 --> 01:01:52,880
 So I had done films--

1726
01:01:52,880 --> 01:01:54,040
 I have to join this month.

1727
01:01:54,040 --> 01:01:55,320
 --in Texas.

1728
01:01:55,320 --> 01:01:57,880
 And I had done films in New York.

1729
01:01:57,880 --> 01:01:59,000
 But not a lot.

1730
01:01:59,000 --> 01:02:00,240
 Mostly it was theater.

1731
01:02:00,240 --> 01:02:03,200
 So when I moved here and I got Pat--

1732
01:02:03,200 --> 01:02:04,560
 I got Barnaby Jones.

1733
01:02:04,560 --> 01:02:08,120
 That was my second job.

1734
01:02:08,120 --> 01:02:12,440
 I had to get out of the car and run towards Buddy Ebsen

1735
01:02:12,440 --> 01:02:14,720
 and then stop and do my line.

1736
01:02:14,720 --> 01:02:17,280
 And so Pat Hingle said--

1737
01:02:17,280 --> 01:02:19,560
 and I kept missing the mark because you

1738
01:02:19,560 --> 01:02:22,360
 can't have to look down.

1739
01:02:22,360 --> 01:02:23,880
 And Pat Hingle said, come here.

1740
01:02:23,880 --> 01:02:24,400
 I said, what?

1741
01:02:24,400 --> 01:02:26,360
 He said, ask for a sandbag.

1742
01:02:26,360 --> 01:02:27,560
 And I go, oh.

1743
01:02:27,560 --> 01:02:29,400
 So I said, what's that?

1744
01:02:29,400 --> 01:02:31,120
 He said, you'll see.

1745
01:02:31,120 --> 01:02:32,560
 She needs a sandbag.

1746
01:02:32,560 --> 01:02:34,920
 So they put the sandbag where they wanted me to stop.

1747
01:02:34,920 --> 01:02:35,720
 And your toe--

1748
01:02:35,720 --> 01:02:37,560
 So your toe hits it.

1749
01:02:37,560 --> 01:02:39,280
 And you know that's where you stop.

1750
01:02:39,280 --> 01:02:42,120
 But unless you know these things or somebody

1751
01:02:42,120 --> 01:02:44,240
 teaches you these things, you're on the set

1752
01:02:44,240 --> 01:02:46,760
 looking like an idiot, like I was.

1753
01:02:46,760 --> 01:02:50,800
 So you've got to know your game.

1754
01:02:50,800 --> 01:02:52,360
 Because if you get on a set, I've

1755
01:02:52,360 --> 01:02:54,440
 seen people that don't know how to make their mark.

1756
01:02:54,440 --> 01:02:57,680
 They don't know they have to match their blocking.

1757
01:02:57,680 --> 01:03:00,320
 There's a master in their close ups and over the shoulder.

1758
01:03:00,320 --> 01:03:02,880
 If you don't know how, you've got to match it.

1759
01:03:02,880 --> 01:03:05,120
 And if you pick up this Ouija board with the right hand,

1760
01:03:05,120 --> 01:03:06,720
 you've got to do it every time with the right hand.

1761
01:03:06,720 --> 01:03:08,480
 You can't do it with the left hand.

1762
01:03:08,480 --> 01:03:11,800
 And so I've seen people get fired on set so much

1763
01:03:11,800 --> 01:03:13,600
 because they weren't trained.

1764
01:03:13,600 --> 01:03:17,080
 They just-- they didn't know what the protocol was.

1765
01:03:17,080 --> 01:03:17,880
 Just fired.

1766
01:03:17,880 --> 01:03:19,160
 And then they're out.

1767
01:03:19,160 --> 01:03:19,800
 Oh my god.

1768
01:03:19,800 --> 01:03:20,840
 I remember one time--

1769
01:03:20,840 --> 01:03:23,520
 When you're seen as hard to work with.

1770
01:03:23,520 --> 01:03:25,160
 One time, I played a prison guard.

1771
01:03:25,160 --> 01:03:29,840
 And somebody goes, he would look really cool smoking cigarettes.

1772
01:03:29,840 --> 01:03:31,520
 And I was like, all right.

1773
01:03:31,520 --> 01:03:33,360
 And they had given me cigarettes.

1774
01:03:33,360 --> 01:03:35,320
 And I was like thinking it was cool.

1775
01:03:35,320 --> 01:03:38,160
 I got through the first one because they're fake cigarettes.

1776
01:03:38,160 --> 01:03:40,160
 Next thing you know, we're shooting for like two days

1777
01:03:40,160 --> 01:03:42,520
 in prison guards smoking cigarettes all day long.

1778
01:03:42,520 --> 01:03:44,280
 And I was like, god, I hate that person.

1779
01:03:44,280 --> 01:03:46,960
 Just mention that you had to smoke cigarettes

1780
01:03:46,960 --> 01:03:49,960
 because you have to every time have a cigarette in your hand.

1781
01:03:49,960 --> 01:03:55,440
 But what's funny is there's a movie back in the day called

1782
01:03:55,440 --> 01:03:56,320
 Belly.

1783
01:03:56,320 --> 01:03:58,520
 And they're smoking a huge blunt.

1784
01:03:58,520 --> 01:04:00,760
 But with weed in it, you know what a blunt is, obviously.

1785
01:04:00,760 --> 01:04:02,720
 So they're smoking it in each scene.

1786
01:04:02,720 --> 01:04:03,560
 It's this big.

1787
01:04:03,560 --> 01:04:04,560
 And then it's this big.

1788
01:04:04,560 --> 01:04:05,360
 And it's this big.

1789
01:04:05,360 --> 01:04:08,760
 And I swore I was so excited when I saw myself smoking

1790
01:04:08,760 --> 01:04:11,520
 the cigarettes because they went from this big to this big.

1791
01:04:11,520 --> 01:04:13,360
 There's no stopping.

1792
01:04:13,360 --> 01:04:14,840
 It's called continuity, right?

1793
01:04:14,840 --> 01:04:15,680
 Continuity.

1794
01:04:15,680 --> 01:04:17,080
 Continuity is very important.

1795
01:04:17,080 --> 01:04:19,080
 And on the professional sets, there's

1796
01:04:19,080 --> 01:04:20,520
 somebody there to check all that.

1797
01:04:20,520 --> 01:04:23,520
 Yeah, you have script advisors and you've got continuity.

1798
01:04:23,520 --> 01:04:24,400
 Real doctors.

1799
01:04:24,400 --> 01:04:27,440
 We had real doctors on the show house

1800
01:04:27,440 --> 01:04:30,440
 all the time to make sure we were doing it.

1801
01:04:30,440 --> 01:04:33,920
 I did a-- the film that didn't get released,

1802
01:04:33,920 --> 01:04:37,400
 he's one of my best friends, was the director, Kaya.

1803
01:04:37,400 --> 01:04:43,240
 But we shot-- for continuity, we shot a prison scene

1804
01:04:43,240 --> 01:04:44,840
 where he shanks me.

1805
01:04:44,840 --> 01:04:45,800
 It's really gruesome.

1806
01:04:45,800 --> 01:04:47,640
 I'll show you afterwards if you want to see it.

1807
01:04:47,640 --> 01:04:48,800
 I haven't watched it in a while.

1808
01:04:48,800 --> 01:04:52,000
 But when they come walking in, my character's

1809
01:04:52,000 --> 01:04:55,200
 kind of like the big white shot collar guy.

1810
01:04:55,200 --> 01:04:56,840
 And I'm like, no, go figure.

1811
01:04:56,840 --> 01:04:58,720
 And they put all these fake tattoos all over me.

1812
01:04:58,720 --> 01:05:00,960
 It looks super cool.

1813
01:05:00,960 --> 01:05:04,960
 And I thought it'd be cool to-- they saw me warming up

1814
01:05:04,960 --> 01:05:07,840
 and doing dips on the edge of the bench.

1815
01:05:07,840 --> 01:05:09,280
 They're like, oh, that looks dope.

1816
01:05:09,280 --> 01:05:12,600
 As we pan across you, you're going to be in there

1817
01:05:12,600 --> 01:05:14,040
 pumping your arms up.

1818
01:05:14,040 --> 01:05:15,520
 And I'm like, yeah, sure, let's do it.

1819
01:05:15,520 --> 01:05:17,360
 I was a big bodybuilder at the time.

1820
01:05:17,360 --> 01:05:19,480
 And after about four or five takes,

1821
01:05:19,480 --> 01:05:24,120
 and I've done 150 dips, my arms were locking up.

1822
01:05:24,120 --> 01:05:25,320
 I couldn't move anymore.

1823
01:05:25,320 --> 01:05:27,080
 I was like, continuity means a different thing

1824
01:05:27,080 --> 01:05:28,280
 when you're actually pushing.

1825
01:05:28,280 --> 01:05:29,160
 That's so funny.

1826
01:05:29,160 --> 01:05:32,320
 I know, but my triceps were fucking huge.

1827
01:05:32,320 --> 01:05:33,680
 But I got up.

1828
01:05:33,680 --> 01:05:34,640
 My arms were locked.

1829
01:05:34,640 --> 01:05:37,200
 And I was like, ah, I can't move my arms.

1830
01:05:37,200 --> 01:05:39,000
 Because I just had to keep doing it.

1831
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:40,720
 Because otherwise, you get one take that's

1832
01:05:40,720 --> 01:05:41,720
 completely different.

1833
01:05:41,720 --> 01:05:44,120
 Yeah, I mean, it looks easy.

1834
01:05:44,120 --> 01:05:46,480
 Our job is to make it look easy.

1835
01:05:46,480 --> 01:05:47,000
 Yeah, exactly.

1836
01:05:47,000 --> 01:05:47,840
 But it ain't easy.

1837
01:05:47,840 --> 01:05:48,480
 It ain't easy.

